WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.060 --> 00:00:03.270
- I get my best performance

00:00:03.270 --> 00:00:06.401
when there's like a meaningful object,

00:00:06.401 --> 00:00:07.980
like in the set

00:00:07.980 --> 00:00:09.120
or like in the scene.

00:00:09.120 --> 00:00:10.320
- Did you use that for the film?

00:00:10.320 --> 00:00:12.277
- No, 'cause we were alone.

00:00:12.277 --> 00:00:13.110
- All alone.

00:00:13.110 --> 00:00:15.033
We were alone in a recording booth.

00:00:16.315 --> 00:00:18.815
(light music)

00:00:20.709 --> 00:00:22.110
- I took from my parents a little bit

00:00:22.110 --> 00:00:23.250
'cause they're theater kids.

00:00:23.250 --> 00:00:24.390
They met in theater

00:00:24.390 --> 00:00:26.790
and then they created a theater kid

00:00:26.790 --> 00:00:28.110
that got to play a theater kid.

00:00:28.110 --> 00:00:31.140
So Margot is really big and expressive

00:00:31.140 --> 00:00:33.180
and loud and every moment is the moment.

00:00:33.180 --> 00:00:34.920
It's curtain call at all times.

00:00:34.920 --> 00:00:37.530
She is on stage at all times.

00:00:37.530 --> 00:00:39.360
She's, you know, producing,

00:00:39.360 --> 00:00:41.130
directing her friends at all times.

00:00:41.130 --> 00:00:42.480
She's just a nut.

00:00:42.480 --> 00:00:44.610
- Oh, life is not a dress rehearsal.

00:00:44.610 --> 00:00:46.890
It's time for you to go big

00:00:46.890 --> 00:00:47.970
and go

00:00:47.970 --> 00:00:49.590
to prom.

00:00:49.590 --> 00:00:51.730
- So I spent a lot of my summertime

00:00:52.620 --> 00:00:56.160
at my parents' cottage
and there's a big rock

00:00:56.160 --> 00:00:58.470
by the lake and I would spend like

00:00:58.470 --> 00:01:01.080
a lot of time lounging on the rock,

00:01:01.080 --> 00:01:03.000
willing myself to become a mermaid.

00:01:03.000 --> 00:01:06.190
Just being like, "Come on, grow a tail."

00:01:06.190 --> 00:01:09.540
- I'm a mother flipping mermaid.

00:01:09.540 --> 00:01:12.318
- So I did that for a while,
so I feel like I would,

00:01:12.318 --> 00:01:15.660
I feel like I had to
draw something from that.

00:01:15.660 --> 00:01:17.760
- Ruby gets like overwhelmed very quickly.

00:01:17.760 --> 00:01:19.380
She spirals very easily.

00:01:19.380 --> 00:01:22.380
That's something as a
performer, fun to play.

00:01:22.380 --> 00:01:25.080
It's so tough because the physicality

00:01:25.080 --> 00:01:27.840
when you're in a recording booth

00:01:27.840 --> 00:01:29.430
you don't have a lot of freedom there

00:01:29.430 --> 00:01:31.080
because you don't wanna move too much

00:01:31.080 --> 00:01:33.540
because you don't wanna
like have the fabric pick up

00:01:33.540 --> 00:01:35.820
on any of the mics and you don't wanna,

00:01:35.820 --> 00:01:37.560
you know, move away from the mics,

00:01:37.560 --> 00:01:40.614
but to me, I found that
if I was able to do

00:01:40.614 --> 00:01:44.010
like even just like wrap
my limbs like together

00:01:44.010 --> 00:01:47.160
or hold myself a little,
it helped my performance.

00:01:47.160 --> 00:01:49.908
I knew that they were
gonna try and animate her

00:01:49.908 --> 00:01:52.375
kind of in that capacity.

00:01:52.375 --> 00:01:55.080
Oh, I hope my performance
was better because of it.

00:01:55.080 --> 00:01:58.023
- Ruby Gillman, teenage kraken.

00:01:59.407 --> 00:02:01.490
(laughs)

